  "implementation": [
    "native domain has separate live/exited/cancelled states; lease Drop never overwrites cancellation",
    "queued Promise/nextTick/GC-destroy/finalization/uncaught jobs are removed and their managed roots released; cancellation does not invoke their callbacks",
    "late enqueue preserves cancelled owner identity rather than adopting into the settling sibling",
    "finalization cleanup roots all extracted registry/record pairs before removing records and allocating",
    "C callback recognizes CANCEL before normal subtask/read dispatch",
    "runtime task_cancel completes its finite error boundary before canonical subtask.cancel can suspend",
    "native children unjoin before synchronous cancellation; typed argument buffers and rooted frames remain valid until acknowledgement",
    "only a successful return marks the result area initialized, including a return winning cancellation; cancellation statuses skip result free",
    "cancelled tasks are omitted from C wake scans while native cancellation may let siblings run",
    "children and task frames release after acknowledgement, followed by canonical task.cancel and EXIT; public DriverCall drop policy remains Store retirement"
  ],
  "prototypeFindings": [
